  "preamble": "In Northern Wu, which keeps the Middle Chinese voiced obstruent series, the voiced alveolo-palatal affricate [dʑ] of the 常/禪 initial became the voiced alveolar fricative [z], losing affrication and palatality but keeping voicing. Mandarin, Cantonese and Hakka devoiced the same initial; the numeral 十 'ten' is a Shanghainese exception with voiceless [səʔ⁵⁵].",
